NNAAMMEE
     kkttrrdduummpp — print kernel ktr trace buffer

SSYYNNOOPPSSIISS
     kkttrrdduummpp [--ccffllqqrrttHH] [--ii _k_t_r_f_i_l_e] [--MM _c_o_r_e] [--NN _s_y_s_t_e_m] [--oo _o_u_t_f_i_l_e]

DDEESSCCRRIIPPTTIIOONN
     The kkttrrdduummpp utility is used to dump the contents of the kernel ktr trace
     buffer.

     The following options are available:

     --cc          Print the CPU number that each entry was logged from.

     --ll          Poll the kernel ktr trace buffer periodically dumping any new
                 events after each poll.

     --ff          Print the file and line number that each entry was logged
                 from.

     --qq          Quiet mode; do not print the column header.

     --rr          Print relative timestamps rather than absolute timestamps.

     --tt          Print the timestamp for each entry.

     --HH          Print the thread ID for each entry.

     --ii _k_t_r_f_i_l_e  File containing saved ktr trace events; for more information
                 see the ktr(4) manual page.

     --NN _s_y_s_t_e_m   The kernel image to resolve symbols from.  The default is the
                 value returned via getbootfile(3).

     --MM _c_o_r_e     The core file or memory image to read from.  The default is
                 _/_d_e_v_/_m_e_m.

     --oo _o_u_t_f_i_l_e  The file to write the output to.  The default is standard
                 output.

SSEEEE AALLSSOO
